@slim: 1.0s
@+name: pptx
@+desc: Use any time a .pptx file is involved — creating, reading, editing, combining. Trigger on "deck", "slides", "presentation", .pptx filename.

# Quick Reference
| Task                  | Method |
| Read/analyze content  | `python -m markitdown presentation.pptx` |
| Edit from template    | Read editing.md |
| Create from scratch   | Read pptxgenjs.md |

# Reading
=== READ_CMDS [bash]
python -m markitdown presentation.pptx
python scripts/thumbnail.py presentation.pptx
python scripts/office/unpack.py presentation.pptx unpacked/
=== /READ_CMDS

# Editing
Read editing.md. Steps: analyze template → unpack → edit → clean → pack

# Design Rules

## Before Starting
- Bold content-informed palette (swappable = not specific enough)
- Dominance: one color 60-70%, 1-2 support, one sharp accent
- Contrast: dark for title+conclusion, light for content. Or all-dark throughout.
- One visual motif repeated on every slide

## Color Palettes
| Theme              | Primary          | Secondary        | Accent  |
| Midnight Executive | 1E2761 navy      | CADCFC ice-blue  | FFFFFF  |
| Forest & Moss      | 2C5F2D forest    | 97BC62 moss      | F5F5F5  |
| Coral Energy       | F96167 coral     | F9E795 gold      | 2F3C7E  |
| Warm Terracotta    | B85042           | E7E8D1 sand      | A7BEAE  |
| Ocean Gradient     | 065A82 deep-blue | 1C7293 teal      | 21295C  |
| Charcoal Minimal   | 36454F           | F2F2F2 off-white | 212121  |
| Teal Trust         | 028090           | 00A896 seafoam   | 02C39A  |
| Berry & Cream      | 6D2E46 berry     | A26769 dusty-rose| ECE2D0  |
| Sage Calm          | 84B59F sage      | 69A297           | 50808E  |
| Cherry Bold        | 990011 cherry    | FCF6F5 off-white | 2F3C7E  |

## Per-Slide
- Every slide needs a visual: image, chart, icon, or shape
- Layouts: two-column, icon+text rows, 2x2/2x3 grid, half-bleed image
- Data: large stat callouts (60-72pt numbers), comparison columns, timeline/flow

## Typography
| Header Font  | Body Font     |
| Georgia      | Calibri       |
| Arial Black  | Arial         |
| Calibri      | Calibri Light |
| Trebuchet MS | Calibri       |
| Impact       | Arial         |
| Palatino     | Garamond      |

| Element        | Size        |
| Title          | 36-44pt bold |
| Section header | 20-24pt bold |
| Body           | 14-16pt     |
| Captions       | 10-12pt     |

## Avoid
- Repeating layouts across slides
- Centered body text (left-align; center titles only)
- Titles <36pt
- Default blue — pick topic-specific colors
- Text-only slides
- Accent lines under titles [AI tell — never use]

# QA (Required — Assume Problems)

## Content Check
=== QA_CMDS [bash]
python -m markitdown output.pptx
python -m markitdown output.pptx | grep -iE "xxxx|lorem|ipsum|this.*(page|slide).*layout"
=== /QA_CMDS

## Visual QA
Use subagents — fresh eyes. Convert to images then inspect:

=== VISUAL_PROMPT
Visually inspect these slides. Assume issues exist — find them.
Look for: overlapping elements, text overflow, lines misaligned for wrapped titles,
citations colliding with content, gaps <0.3", margins <0.5", misaligned columns,
low-contrast text or icons, excessive wrapping, leftover placeholders.
List issues per slide, including minor ones.
=== /VISUAL_PROMPT

## Loop
1. Generate → convert → inspect
2. List all issues (none found = look harder)
3. Fix → re-verify affected slides only
4. Repeat until clean pass

# Convert to Images
=== CONVERT [bash]
python scripts/office/soffice.py --headless --convert-to pdf output.pptx
pdftoppm -jpeg -r 150 output.pdf slide
=== /CONVERT

# Dependencies
- `pip install "markitdown[pptx]"` — text extraction
- `pip install Pillow` — thumbnails
- `npm install -g pptxgenjs` — create from scratch
- LibreOffice soffice — PDF conversion
- Poppler pdftoppm — PDF to images
